# website-clones workspace

This workspace clones websites using a **generator** model:

- `ai-website-cloner-template/` — the GENERATOR. Holds upstream agent tooling and
  the base Next.js scaffold. Tracks official updates — **do not edit it**.
- `sites/<name>/` — a generated site (its own git repo). Website project only:
  runnable Next.js app + allowed clone artifacts. Never generator tooling.
  Docker/ops files only if created with `--with-docker`.
- `scripts/` — workspace automation (bootstrap, new-site, batch-clone, update-*,
  build-clone-command, check).
- `.cursor/` — workspace Cursor config (`/clone-website`, rules, Playwright MCP).
  Customize `.cursor/commands/clone-website.override.md`; rebuild with
  `scripts/build-clone-command.sh` (never hand-edit `clone-website.md`).
  Pin Playwright in `.cursor/playwright-mcp.version` (synced into `mcp.json`).

## What may live in `sites/<name>/`

**Allowed (website project):**
- `src/`, `public/`, `package.json`, lockfile, build configs
- `docs/research/`, `docs/design-references/` — clone specs & screenshots
- `scripts/download-assets.mjs` — one-off asset download helper during clone
- Docker files only when scaffolded with `--with-docker`
- `CLONE_TARGETS.txt`, `.generator-version`

**Forbidden (generator / agent tooling):**
- `.claude/`, `.cursor/`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `GEMINI.md`
- `sync-agent-rules.sh`, `sync-skills.mjs`, and other multi-platform sync files

## Cloning a website

1. `scripts/bootstrap-template.sh` once (if generator missing)
2. `scripts/new-site.sh <name> <url>` (requires Node.js 24+; see root `.nvmrc` /
   `package.json` engines — scripts try nvm → fnm → asdf)
3. Open / work in `sites/<name>/`
4. Run `/clone-website <url>` — skill paths are **relative to the site root**
5. Browser automation: Playwright MCP in `.cursor/mcp.json` (from version pin)

Only clone sites you own or are authorized to reproduce. No phishing or brand impersonation.

## Website tech stack (inside each site)

- Next.js 16 (App Router, React 19, TypeScript strict) — breaking changes;
  consult `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing code
- shadcn/ui (Radix primitives, Tailwind CSS v4, `cn()` utility)
- Tailwind CSS v4 with oklch design tokens; Lucide React icons

## Commands (run inside a site)

- `npm run dev` / `npm run build` / `npm run lint` / `npm run typecheck` / `npm run check`

## Code style

- TypeScript strict, no `any`; named exports; PascalCase components, camelCase utils
- Tailwind utility classes, no inline styles; 2-space indent; mobile-first responsive

## Design principles

- Pixel-perfect emulation — match spacing, colors, typography exactly
- Real content — use the target's actual text and assets, not placeholders
- Match 1:1 first, customize later
